  "generated_text": "Let $D$ be the foot of the altitude from $B$ to $AC$, and $E$ be the foot of the altitude from $A$ to $BC$. Then $CD = 3$, $AD = 5$, $CE = 2$, and $BE = x$.\n\nBy the Pythagorean Theorem, we have:\n\\[ AD^2 + CD^2 = AC^2 \\Rightarrow 5^2 + 3^2 = AC^2 \\Rightarrow 25 + 9 = AC^2 \\Rightarrow AC^2 = 34 \\Rightarrow AC = \\sqrt{34} \\]\n\nBy the Pythagorean Theorem again, we have:\n\\[ BE^2 + CE^2 = BC^2 \\Rightarrow x^2 + 2^2 = BC^2 \\Rightarrow x^2 + 4 = BC^2 \\]\n\nSince $AC = \\sqrt{34}$ and $BC = \\sqrt{34}$, we have:\n\\[ AC^2 = BC^2 \\Rightarrow 34 = x^2 + 4 \\Rightarrow x^2 = 30 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\]",
